{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Sample code","anchor":"Sample-code","identifiers":["doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/OATHSampleCode","doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/PIVToolSampleCode"],"generated":true}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The interceptor demonstrates how to:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Intercept "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"navigator.credentials.create()"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"navigator.credentials.get()"},{"type":"text","text":" in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WKWebView"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Round-trip WebAuthn Level 3 JSON directly into the SDK’s "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Registration\/Options","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Authentication\/Options","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" types."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Drive the SDK’s high-level "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" ceremony without hand-rolling CTAP2 plumbing, PIN retry, or extension wiring."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the bundled "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FidoUI"},{"type":"text","text":" module for transport selection (USB-C \/ Lightning \/ NFC on iOS, HID on macOS) and for the PIN, UV, error, and success panels."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"By bypassing WebKit’s built-in WebAuthn implementation you get full control over which authenticator handles the request, the look and feel of the prompts, and access to extensions that the platform doesn’t otherwise surface.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Architecture-Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Architecture Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The sample itself is intentionally thin:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Interceptor.js"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — injected into the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WKWebView"},{"type":"text","text":" to monkey-patch "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"navigator.credentials.{create,get}"},{"type":"text","text":" and shuttle requests\/responses through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WKScriptMessageHandler"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"WebView.swift"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIViewRepresentable"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSViewRepresentable"},{"type":"text","text":" wrapper that installs the script, registers message handlers, and coordinates ceremony lifecycle (cancel on dismiss, cancel-and-replace on a new request)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"WebAuthnHandler.swift"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — decodes the JSON envelope and calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FidoUI.makeCredential"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FidoUI.getAssertion"},{"type":"text","text":" with the WebView’s origin."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ContentView.swift"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — minimal SwiftUI shell with a URL bar and back button."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"FidoUI"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (separate Swift package under "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Samples\/WebAuthnInterceptorSample\/FidoUI"},{"type":"text","text":") — the reusable UI + transport layer described below."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The end-to-end flow:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Page JS calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"navigator.credentials.create()"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".get()"},{"type":"text","text":"; the interceptor serializes the options as WebAuthn Level 3 JSON and posts it to Swift."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WebAuthnHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" decodes the JSON straight into the SDK’s strongly-typed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Options"},{"type":"text","text":" and hands them to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FidoUI"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FidoUI"},{"type":"text","text":" opens a transport, runs the ceremony via "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and shows PIN \/ UV \/ error \/ success panels as needed."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The resulting "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Registration\/Response","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Authentication\/Response","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is serialized via its built-in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"toJSON()"},{"type":"text","text":" and posted back to JS."}]}]}]},{"anchor":"Intercepting-WebAuthn-Calls","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Intercepting WebAuthn Calls"},{"anchor":"JavaScript-Injection","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"JavaScript Injection"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Interceptor.js","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" replaces ","type":"text"},{"code":"navigator.credentials.create","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"navigator.credentials.get","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with versions that forward to Swift. Binary fields (","type":"text"},{"code":"challenge","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"user.id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"rawId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", …) are serialized to ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"base64url"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" strings via ","type":"text"},{"code":"JSON.stringify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with a replacer — this matches the WebAuthn Level 3 JSON format the SDK consumes natively, so no custom binary-wrapping protocol is needed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"javascript","type":"codeListing","code":["function interceptWebAuthn(type, options, originalFn) {","    if (!shouldIntercept(options)) return originalFn(options);","","    return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {","        pendingResolve = resolve;","        pendingReject = reject;","","        const publicKey = serializePublicKeyOptionsToJSON(options.publicKey);","        if (type === 'create' && publicKey.rp && !publicKey.rp.id) {","            publicKey.rp.id = window.location.hostname;","        }","","        const request = { type, request: publicKey };","        window.webkit.messageHandlers[`__webauthn_${type}__`]","            .postMessage(JSON.stringify(request));","    });","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The script is injected at document start so it runs before any page code:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let script = WKUserScript(","    source: interceptorScript,","    injectionTime: .atDocumentStart,","    forMainFrameOnly: true",")","config.userContentController.addUserScript(script)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"shouldIntercept","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" returns "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for any "},{"code":"publicKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"-bearing request, but is the natural seam for narrower policies (e.g. only intercept when "},{"code":"publicKey.hints","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" includes "},{"code":"\"security-key\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Receiving-Messages-in-Swift","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Receiving Messages in Swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"Coordinator","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is both "},{"code":"WKNavigationDelegate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"WKScriptMessageHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". It accepts requests from the main frame and derives their origin from WebKit. Each request starts a fresh ceremony and cancels any in-flight one first."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"shutdown()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is called from "},{"code":"dismantle{UI,NS}View","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" so navigating away mid-ceremony unwinds the open NFC\/HID handle."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Driving-the-Ceremony","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Driving the Ceremony"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The WebView derives the origin from the requesting main frame’s "},{"code":"WKSecurityOrigin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and passes it to "},{"code":"WebAuthnHandler","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The handler decodes the envelope and delegates to "},{"code":"FidoUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["struct WebAuthnRequest<Options: Decodable>: Decodable {","    let publicKey: Options","    enum CodingKeys: String, CodingKey { case publicKey = \"request\" }","}","","func handleCreate(_ data: Data, origin: WebAuthn.Origin) async throws -> String {","    let request = try JSONDecoder().decode(","        WebAuthnRequest<WebAuthn.Registration.Options>.self,","        from: data","    )","    let response = try await fidoUI.makeCredential(","        request.publicKey,","        origin: origin,","        serviceName: origin.host","    )","    return String(decoding: try response.toJSON(), as: UTF8.self)","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"handleGet","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the symmetric counterpart that decodes "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Authentication\/Options"},{"type":"text","text":" and calls "},{"code":"fidoUI.getAssertion","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The response JSON produced by "},{"code":"toJSON()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is already in WebAuthn Level 3 format with base64url-encoded binary fields, so the JS side just decodes those back to "},{"code":"ArrayBuffer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when it materializes the credential."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Returning-the-Response-to-JavaScript","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Returning the Response to JavaScript"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Swift-side response is JSON-encoded, base64-wrapped for the bridge, and handed back via a callback installed by the interceptor:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let encodedResponse = Data(response.utf8).base64EncodedString()","_ = try? await webView?.evaluateJavaScript(","    \"__webauthn_callback__('\\(encodedResponse)')\"",")"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"JavaScript decodes the JSON and rebuilds a "},{"code":"PublicKeyCredential","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"-shaped object — converting the base64url binary fields back to "},{"code":"ArrayBuffer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s and wiring up "},{"code":"getClientExtensionResults","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"getAuthenticatorData","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"getPublicKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"toJSON","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and the rest. Errors travel through a parallel "},{"code":"__webauthn_error__","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" channel and surface to the page as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DOMException"},{"type":"text","text":" with name "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NotAllowedError"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-FidoUI-Module","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The FidoUI Module"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FidoUI"},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@MainActor"},{"type":"text","text":" Swift package shipped alongside the sample, and it does most of the work. Intercepting "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"navigator.credentials.*"},{"type":"text","text":" means giving up the platform’s built-in WebAuthn sheets (tap prompt, PIN entry, errors, success) — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FidoUI"},{"type":"text","text":" replaces them end-to-end with a complete ceremony UI: connect \/ touch, PIN entry with retry counters, PIN change, first-time PIN setup, forced PIN-change recovery, fingerprint enrollment, credential picker, and error \/ success results. The host app stays a thin shell."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Beyond the panels, it owns the moving parts that you’d otherwise re-implement per app:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Transport selection.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" On iOS it tries wired (USB-C \/ Lightning) first and falls back to NFC. On macOS it defaults to HID FIDO, with optional USB CCID through "},{"code":"wiredTransport","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Connections are polled and reused across a ceremony."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Ceremony serialization.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Concurrent calls on the same "},{"code":"FidoUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instance are queued so they don’t fight over the alert window, transport, or shared panel state."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Cancellation.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" A single "},{"code":"cancel()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" call (used by the WebView coordinator on dismiss \/ new message) tears down the active transport and dismisses any visible panel."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FidoUI"},{"type":"text","text":" instance per host with a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"presentationAnchor"},{"type":"text","text":" closure and an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isPublicSuffix"},{"type":"text","text":" checker. Capture the initiating view weakly and return its window. The closure runs when each queued ceremony starts. If the window is unavailable, the call throws "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FidoUI.Error.presentationUnavailable"},{"type":"text","text":" before opening a transport."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"makeCredential"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"getAssertion"},{"type":"text","text":" for each request. The relying party must verify the returned response before completing registration or sign-in. See "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Samples\/WebAuthnInterceptorSample\/FidoUI\/"},{"type":"text","text":" for the full source."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Platform-Notes","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Platform Notes"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"iOS.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The wired path goes through CryptoTokenKit ("},{"code":"WiredSmartCardConnection","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — USB-C or Lightning), and the NFC path through "},{"code":"NFCSmartCardConnection","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The sample’s "},{"code":"Info.plist","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" declares "},{"code":"NFCReaderUsageDescription","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and lists the FIDO applet AID ("},{"code":"A0000006472F0001","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") under "},{"code":"com.apple.developer.nfc.readersession.iso7816.select-identifiers","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; the entitlements turn on "},{"code":"com.apple.developer.nfc.readersession.formats","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"TAG","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") and "},{"code":"com.apple.security.smartcard","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"macOS.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"FidoUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" defaults to "},{"code":"HIDFIDOConnection","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Launch the sample with "},{"code":"--ccid","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to use "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/USBSmartCardConnection"},{"type":"text","text":" and optionally "},{"code":"--ccid-reader \"<reader name>\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to select a reader. The key must support CTAP2 over USB CCID. The sample enables "},{"code":"com.apple.security.smartcard","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"com.apple.security.device.usb","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for these transports."}]}]}]},{"anchor":"Where-to-Customize","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Where to Customize"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Which requests get intercepted."}]},{"text":" Edit ","type":"text"},{"code":"shouldIntercept","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Interceptor.js","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to scope by hint, RP ID, or any other heuristic.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origin verification."}]},{"text":" The WebView uses the main frame’s security origin and rejects requests from child frames. Replace the ","type":"text"},{"code":"isPublicSuffix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" closure passed to ","type":"text"},{"code":"FidoUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with a real public-suffix-list check before shipping.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"UI."}]},{"text":" Swap or restyle the panels in ","type":"text"},{"code":"FidoUI\/Sources\/FidoUI\/Views\/","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the rest of the module is UI-agnostic.","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This sample shows how to build a FIDO2\/WebAuthn client that intercepts "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"navigator.credentials.{create,get}"},{"type":"text","text":" calls inside a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WKWebView"},{"type":"text","text":" and routes them to a YubiKey. It uses the high-lev